+Builders should be able to connect to any of the infrastructure providers' peering services below. They have committed to offer high-quality peering services to the public for a reasonable price. If any of the peering services listed below do not meet this committment, please notify the Foundation team via email (bugbounty [at] hyperfoundation [dot] org).
+Available peers for builders to connect to
+Allium -
+https://docs.allium.so/nodes/hyperliquid-sentry-peer
+Dwellir -
+https://www.dwellir.com/docs/hyperliquid/peering
+Hydromancer -
+https://docs.hydromancer.xyz/peering
+Hyperdash -
+https://docs.hyperdash.com/data/direct-sentry-peering
+Quicknode -
+https://www.quicknode.com/hyperliquid-peering
+Eligibility
+To further reduce the barrier to entry for obtaining high-quality onchain data, the Foundation non-validating node is open to high-quality infrastructure providers as a reliable peer.
+Reputable infrastructure provider with track record of excellent SLAs, used by a diverse set of builders. Criteria for consideration include: minimum operating history of 1 year as an infrastructure provider, with a minimum of 100 clients operated across 5 distinct networks/protocols, and no history of a peering or service agreement terminated for cause by another network or foundation in the preceding 3 months.
+Uptime of 99.9%.
+Open access with non-discriminatory pricing. The current benchmark price is less than $1k/month, which covers compute and egress costs.
+Auto-scaling with number of peers connected to the service.
+No preferential treatment of specific clients (e.g., market makers).
+Apply
+If you are eligible, you may fill out the
+form
+.
